[00:09.03]Can I share a little secret?
[00:13.39]Not to insinuate some grand misgivings, I-
[00:17.83]I just don't know who else could keep it
[00:22.32]And you're the only one that might forgive me, I-
[00:26.89]I don't like the way my clothes fit
[00:31.07]And I don't like the way I sound when silence comes
[00:35.32]I thought that sharing it could close it
[00:39.64]But nothing ever seems to happen when I want
[00:43.74][01:05.59][01:58.46][03:25.32][03:47.29]
[00:45.27][03:26.71]Oh god, if I could change
[00:48.59][03:30.01](To be anything I can't be)
[00:51.20][03:32.42]Or everything could stay the same
[00:52.99][03:34.36](Simply rotting in a lifesized landfill, ah)
[00:55.68][03:37.35]Living just to change
[00:57.34][03:38.64](Is there something that I should be?)
[00:59.66][03:41.27]When everything just stays the same
[01:01.81][03:43.06](Tell me quietly so I can't hear you)
[01:23.46]Can I share my biggest secret?
[01:27.66]It's something horrible, or so they tell me, I-
[01:31.93]I hope you won't think of me different
[01:36.09]'Cause nothing scares me more than no more normal, I-
[01:40.66]I hope I don't get any older
[01:45.02]Not 'cause of childhood or my nostalgia, I-
[01:49.39]I'm terrified of my own shoulders
[01:53.73]I'd give up everything to not become this, I-
[02:15.45]Hold my breath
[02:18.33][03:08.46]I stare into the sun
[02:20.52]And wonder if it all could fall to none
[02:24.90]To reach inside my heart
[02:27.01]A million miles apart
[02:29.27]Begging for a different life
[02:33.62]The self that stays unseen
[02:35.84]Someone that could exist outside a dream
[02:40.18][03:15.07]No reply
[02:42.37]I trace along the scars
[02:44.53](No matter what you are, you’re always what you are, I-)
[02:50.21]Close my eyes
[02:53.21]Is anybody there?
[02:55.43]There’s something fundamental I can’t bear
[02:59.74]My fingers at the seams
[03:01.98]A horrible machine
[03:04.18]Begging just to rip it out
[03:10.71]And wonder if it all could come undone
[03:17.17]Do I deserve to die?
[03:19.33]Just tell me I’m a monster in your eyes
